1	/*!
2	This module provides the trait implementations necessary to implement each of
3	the LSP request handlers.
4	
5	Every request handler should live in its own module, with a module name
6	matching the LSP protocol request name as closely as possible. This should be
7	done even when there is tight coupling between multiple request handlers (like
8	type hierarchy) to make it easy to continue to find the right handler given
9	knowledge about the request name.
10	
11	If request handlers need shared helper functions, they can go in a sibling
12	module. For example, see `super::type_hierarchy`.
13	*/
